Subject: [PATCH] ipv6: remove routes retaining an unregistering address device

A live N920I snapshot finds a FIB route with dst.dev=lo but
rt6i_idev->dev=ipsec37 after that MMS interface is unregistered. The old
fib6_ifdown predicate misses it, leaving the IPv6 address-device reference
and netd teardown stuck. Match the address device during unregister too.
Preserve ordinary administrative-down behavior and tolerate absent idev.
Repeated unregister notifications use NETREG_UNREGISTERED in this tree.

This is a targeted 3.10 adaptation of the ownership condition discussed at
https://lkml.iu.edu/1708.1/04771.html; not a verbatim modern-kernel backport.

--- a/net/ipv6/route.c
+++ b/net/ipv6/route.c
@@ -2169,7 +2169,14 @@
 	const struct arg_dev_net *adn = arg;
 	const struct net_device *dev = adn->dev;
 
-	if ((rt->dst.dev == dev || !dev) &&
+	/* Local/cache routes may use loopback for output while retaining the
+	 * address device through rt6i_idev. Include that owner on unregister,
+	 * including repeated notifications after NETREG_UNREGISTERED.
+	 */
+	if ((rt->dst.dev == dev || !dev ||
+	     (rt->rt6i_idev && rt->rt6i_idev->dev == dev &&
+	      (dev->reg_state == NETREG_UNREGISTERING ||
+	       dev->reg_state == NETREG_UNREGISTERED))) &&
 	    rt != adn->net->ipv6.ip6_null_entry)
 		return -1;
 
